# Zara Sales Data Analysis (EDA)

## Project Overview

This project performs **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)** on Zara sales data to uncover meaningful insights, trends, and patterns in customer purchasing behavior.

The main objective is to transform raw data into actionable business insights that can support decision-making.

---

## Objectives

* Understand customer purchasing behavior
* Identify top-performing product categories
* Analyze the relationship between price and sales
* Generate data-driven business recommendations

---

## Dataset

The dataset contains information related to:

* Product categories
* Pricing
* Sales performance
* Customer preferences

---

## Tools & Technologies

* Python 
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Seaborn
* Jupyter Notebook

---

## Analysis Performed

* Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
* Handling Missing Values & Duplicates
* Sales Distribution Analysis
* Category-wise Sales Analysis
* Price vs Sales Relationship
* Correlation Analysis

---

## Key Insights

* Certain product categories contribute significantly to overall sales
* Moderate pricing attracts more customers compared to extreme price ranges
* Sales distribution is uneven, indicating demand variation
* Some variables show strong correlations affecting sales performance

---

## Business Recommendations

* Focus inventory on high-performing product categories
* Optimize pricing strategy to maximize conversions
* Use targeted marketing for popular customer segments
* Improve or re-evaluate low-performing categories

